after Wesberry v. Sanders, challenging Florida's congressional districts. In a 1965 special session the Legislature enacted new boundaries for the 12 districts (Ch. 65-2441), which a federal judge allowed on a temporary basis.","sources":["https://case-law.vlex.com/vid/gong-v-kirk-no-884853427","https://leagle.com/decision/1967411278fsupp1331382"],"districtsChanged":11},"c091":{"why":"researched","kind":"court","text":"In Gong v. Kirk (1967) a three-judge federal court reviewed the 1965 districts under the equal-population rule and set new boundaries for the 12 districts for the 1968 election. The Supreme Court affirmed in Kirk v. Gong (1968).","sources":["https://leagle.com/decision/1967411278fsupp1331382","https://hallapproved.com/us/cases/supreme/1968/1383585/","https://case-law.vlex.com/vid/gong-v-kirk-no-884853427"],"districtsChanged":12},"c093":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 1970 census, which raised Florida's seats from 12 to 15. It was first used in the 1972 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":15},"c098":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 1980 census, which raised Florida's seats from 15 to 19. It was first used in the 1982 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":19},"c103":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 1990 census, which raised Florida's seats from 19 to 23. It was first used in the 1992 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":23},"c105":{"why":"researched","kind":"court","text":"In Johnson v. Mortham (1996) a federal court found that the 3rd District was a racial gerrymander that failed strict scrutiny. The Legislature passed a new plan in May 1996, which the court approved for that year's elections.","sources":["https://www.mnsenate.gov/departments/scr/REDIST/Redsum/flsum.htm"],"districtsChanged":10},"c108":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 2000 census, which raised Florida's seats from 23 to 25. It was first used in the 2002 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":25},"c113":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 2010 census, which raised Florida's seats from 25 to 27. It was first used in the 2012 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial/2020/data/apportionment/apportionment.csv","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":27},"c115":{"why":"event","kind":"court","text":"New map following: Court orders a new congressional map. In League of Women Voters of Florida v. Detzner the Florida Supreme Court found that the 2012 congressional map violated the Fair Districts rules and approved a remedial map in December 2015. It was used from the 2016 election.","sources":["https://redistricting.lls.edu/state/florida/"],"districtsChanged":27},"c118":{"why":"census","kind":"census","text":"New map drawn after the 2020 census, which raised Florida's seats from 27 to 28. It was first used in the 2022 election.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial/2020/data/apportionment/apportionment.csv","https://cdmaps.polisci.ucla.edu/"],"districtsChanged":28},"c120":{"why":"event","kind":"mid-decade","text":"New map following: Mid-decade redistricting. The legislature passed a new congressional map in an April 2026 special session, and the governor signed it on May 4. It redrew 21 of the 28 districts and left Districts 1 through 7 unchanged. Courts declined to block it before the election, and it was used in 2026 while a lawsuit continued.","sources":["https://wusf.org/text/politics-issues/2026-05-06/breakdown-changes-for-florida-new-congressional-map","https://www.wlrn.org/light/government-politics/2026-05-04/desantis-signs-new-congressional-district-map","https://wtop.com/national/2026/06/florida-court-allows-use-of-new-us-house-districts-drawn-by-republicans-for-midterm-elections/"],"districtsChanged":20}}}